Third-party notice - Robert Penner's easing equations / jQuery Easing

One source file of @awacloud/fw, src/io/calc/easing.js, implements Robert
Penner's easing equations in their published (t, b, c, d) form. Its
function bodies are identical in form to the published equations; the
elastic and back families follow the shape of the jQuery Easing v1.3 port
(locally initialised amplitude, period and overshoot). The ESM factory,
JSDoc, tests and every later change are this project's own work.

The two copyright notices and BSD licence texts below are reproduced
verbatim, comment markers included, from jquery.easing.1.3.js in the
upstream repository (https://github.com/gdsmith/jquery.easing, tag v1.3):
the jQuery Easing terms, then the easing-equations terms. Robert Penner's
current terms (MIT and 3-clause BSD) are published at
http://robertpenner.com/easing_terms_of_use.html.
Origin details: docs/dev/provenance.md.

